@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bm-ear-nouns`
IMPORT `bm-ear-period`
IMPORT `bm-ear-fixtures`

-- Tests for the period of insurance (src:40-57). Every expected value was worked by hand
-- from the text and the forks named in NOTES.md section 3, before the assertion was run.
-- A failing assertion here is a finding, never a value to edit.
--
-- Unless a test says otherwise: the works commenced on 5 January 2026, and the schedule
-- ends cover on 31 December 2026.

§ `Tests: the period of insurance`

§§ `Items with a history`

-- Unloaded at the site on 1 February 2026; nothing else has happened to it.
`item A` MEANS `an item with history` 1 FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING

-- As item A, but handed over (as a part) on 1 August 2026.
`item A, handed over on 1 August` MEANS
    `an item with history` 1 FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 8 1))

-- As item A, but its test run was completed on 15 July 2026.
`item A, tested by 15 July` MEANS
    `an item with history` 1 FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 15)) NOTHING NOTHING

-- As item A, but first operated on 20 July 2026.
`item A, operated on 20 July` MEANS
    `an item with history` 1 FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 7 20)) NOTHING

-- A second-hand item whose testing began on 1 July 2026, and the same item if it were new.
`a second-hand item, testing from 1 July` MEANS
    `an item with history` 3 TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
`a new item, testing from 1 July` MEANS
    `an item with history` 3 FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING

§§ `When cover begins (src:42-43; fork F06, F07)`

-- The earlier of works commencement (5 January) and unloading (1 February) starts cover.
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 1 20) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 1 4) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 1 5) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A`
        BECAUSE "the occurrence fell on the day cover began, and the record does not say whether it came before or after"

-- Works not yet commenced: cover on item A starts with its unloading on 1 February.
`works not commenced` MEANS
    `works commenced` NOTHING `testing began` NOTHING `first test operation completed` NOTHING `handed over` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 1 20) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works not commenced`) `for` `item A`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works not commenced`) `for` `item A`
        BECAUSE "the occurrence fell on the day cover began, and the record does not say whether it came before or after"
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 2 2) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works not commenced`) `for` `item A`

-- Neither event has happened: no cover at all.
`item never unloaded` MEANS `an item with history` 1 FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works not commenced`) `for` `item never unloaded`

§§ `Four weeks from the start of testing (src:43-46; forks F08, F09)`

-- Testing began on 1 October 2026. Day 28 after it is 29 October (inside); 30 October is out.
`works testing from 1 October` MEANS
    `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) `testing began` (JUST (YMD 2026 10 1)) `first test operation completed` NOTHING `handed over` NOTHING
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 10 29) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works testing from 1 October`) `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 10 30) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works testing from 1 October`) `for` `item A`
#ASSERT `the last day of the testing period` (`the standard policy with works` `works testing from 1 October`) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 29)

-- "unless otherwise agreed in writing": 60 days agreed. 1 October + 60 days = 30 November.
`the policy with 60 days of testing agreed` MEANS
    `a policy with schedule` `the standard schedule` `works` `works testing from 1 October` `answers` `given, and every answer true and complete`
        `premium paid` TRUE `extension` NOTHING `testing period` (JUST 60) `extra charges agreed` FALSE
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 11 30) `under` `the policy with 60 days of testing agreed` `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 12 1) `under` `the policy with 60 days of testing agreed` `for` `item A`

§§ `First test operation, or handover, whichever is first (src:43-45; fork F07)`

-- The first test operation was completed on 10 October 2026.
`works tested by 10 October` MEANS
    `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) `testing began` (JUST (YMD 2026 10 1)) `first test operation completed` (JUST (YMD 2026 10 10)) `handed over` NOTHING
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 10 9) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works tested by 10 October`) `for` `item A`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 10 10) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works tested by 10 October`) `for` `item A`
        BECAUSE "the occurrence fell on the day of an event that ends cover, and the record does not say which came first"
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 10 11) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works tested by 10 October`) `for` `item A`

-- The works were handed over on 15 September 2026, before any testing.
`works handed over on 15 September` MEANS
    `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) `testing began` NOTHING `first test operation completed` NOTHING `handed over` (JUST (YMD 2026 9 15))
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 9 14) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works handed over on 15 September`) `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 9 20) `under` (`the standard policy with works` `works handed over on 15 September`) `for` `item A`

§§ `The date in the schedule, and an extension (src:56-57; fork F09)`

#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A`

`the policy extended to 31 March 2027` MEANS
    `a policy with schedule` `the standard schedule` `works` `the standard works` `answers` `given, and every answer true and complete`
        `premium paid` TRUE `extension` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 31)) `testing period` NOTHING `extra charges agreed` FALSE
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `under` `the policy extended to 31 March 2027` `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2027 4 1) `under` `the policy extended to 31 March 2027` `for` `item A`

§§ `A part tested, operated or handed over (src:46-51; fork F10)`

#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 8 2) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A, handed over on 1 August`
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 8 2) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 7 16) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A, tested by 15 July`
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 7 14) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A, tested by 15 July`
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 7 21) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `item A, operated on 20 July`

§§ `Second-hand items (src:53-54)`

-- A second-hand item goes off cover when its testing begins; a new item does not.
#ASSERT NOT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `a second-hand item, testing from 1 July`
#ASSERT `the item was on cover on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `for` `a new item, testing from 1 July`

§§ `The period for Part II (src:42-57, 255-256)`

-- A policy whose schedule names only item A, handed over on 1 August 2026.
`the policy naming item A, handed over` MEANS
    `a policy with schedule` (`a schedule with items` (LIST `item A, handed over on 1 August`)) `works` `the standard works`
        `answers` `given, and every answer true and complete` `premium paid` TRUE `extension` NOTHING `testing period` NOTHING `extra charges agreed` FALSE

-- A liability arising from item 1 after it was handed over is off cover; one arising
-- from no particular item is not.
#ASSERT NOT (YMD 2026 8 2) `is within the period of insurance under` `the policy naming item A, handed over` `for a liability arising from item` (JUST 1)
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 8 2) `is within the period of insurance under` `the policy naming item A, handed over` `for a liability arising from item` NOTHING

-- Works not commenced: Part II cover starts with the first unloading of any scheduled item.
`the policy naming item A, works not commenced` MEANS
    `a policy with schedule` (`a schedule with items` (LIST `item A`)) `works` `works not commenced`
        `answers` `given, and every answer true and complete` `premium paid` TRUE `extension` NOTHING `testing period` NOTHING `extra charges agreed` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (YMD 2026 1 20) `is within the period of insurance under` `the policy naming item A, works not commenced` `for a liability arising from item` NOTHING
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 2 20) `is within the period of insurance under` `the policy naming item A, works not commenced` `for a liability arising from item` NOTHING
